"""
## Purpose and audience
Deliberate failing fixture for the spec runner's sibling-describe lane: the
first sibling passes, the second asserts a constant-false comparison so the
runner's ERROR (real failure) outcome class has something honest to detect
across sibling describes. For runner operators and CI owners verifying that
a genuine assertion failure inside the second sibling is classified as
ERROR and not as a crash, a skip, or a pass.
## Operator workflow
./src/compiler_rust/target/bootstrap/simple run test/fixtures/pure_simple_tooling/sibling_describe_red_spec.spl
A healthy run reports 2 executed, 1 failed ("fails deliberately"), with a
non-zero exit code.
## Compatibility and limitations
The second scenario's assertion is intentionally a constant-false literal
comparison; the scorer's pseudo-oracle blocker therefore stays on purpose,
and this file is expected to keep a lower documentization score than a
normal spec. Do not "repair" the comparison — a passing fixture deletes the
only proof the ERROR outcome class works across sibling describes.
## Verification guidance and troubleshooting
A healthy run reports outcome=ERROR, executed=2, failed=1 with "fails
deliberately" among the failures. A pass here means the fixture was
weakened — restore the failing assertion and file a bug against whatever
change made it pass.
"""
# Lifecycle: doc/01_research/domain/sspec_documentization_maintenance.md ;
# doc/03_plan/sspec_modernization_plan.md ;
# doc/04_architecture/sspec_documentization_maintenance.md ;
# doc/05_design/infra/sspec/modern_sspec_typed_evidence_design.md

use std.spec.*

# @manual_section: sibling describe failing fixture
describe "first sibling":
    # @manual scenario evidence
    it "executes first":
        # @req REQ-TEST-RUNNER-SIBLING-002
        # @capture(statistics): executed-example count for the passing sibling
        step("Run the first sibling describe block to completion")
        val first_marker = "first"
        val first_marker_length = first_marker.len()
        expect(first_marker_length).to_equal(5)  # oracle: the passing sibling's marker is the 5-byte literal "first"

describe "second sibling":
    it "fails deliberately":
        # @req REQ-TEST-RUNNER-SIBLING-002
        # @capture(statistics): failed-example count for the ERROR outcome class
        step("Assert an intentionally false comparison so the runner records a failure")
        expect(1).to_equal(2)  # oracle: deliberately false — this fixture exists to fail
